(* fs-records-s2b C5c, the replay-rejected witness, written as a
   correspondence (expected FALSE): "a frame that a Beacon refused at
   sequence t was never accepted by it before" is false: a frame that the
   Beacon accepted at t is delivered again and refused.  FsReceivedFrame and
   FsReceiveRejected carry the frame itself, so the refused frame is the
   accepted one, not merely some frame at an accepted sequence.  The finish
   accepts the response frame at sequence 1, so one receive attempt
   (K_r = 1) exhibits it: the replayed response frame is an old target that
   is not cached and is refused without an open. *)
query s: bitstring, b: bitstring, kid: key_id, root: bitstring, t: nat, f: bitstring,
      i: time, j: time;
  event(FsReceivedFrame(server_to_beacon(), s, b, kid, root, t, f))@i
  && event(FsReceiveRejected(server_to_beacon(), s, b, kid, root, t, f))@j
  ==> j < i.

process FsRecordsS2bMain()
